 {
  "post": 6221,
  "forum": "comp.sys.mac.hardware",
  "lines": [
   {
    "text": "From: \"A•••• J. S••••••\" <a•••••••@nickel.ucs.indiana.edu>",
    "part": "meta",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "Subject: SE/30 Hard Drive Problem",
    "part": "subject",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "Content-Type: text/plain; charset=US-ASCII",
    "part": "meta",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit",
    "part": "meta",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "Organization: Indiana University",
    "part": "meta",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "Mime-Version: 1.0",
    "part": "meta",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "Content-Length: 1161      ",
    "part": "meta",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "Lines: 33",
    "part": "meta",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "I have an SE/30 with a 80 meg HD which dates back to April 1989.  When I",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "originally purchased it, I experienced the failure to boot problem.  This",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "was fixed soon after by a ROM upgrade on the hard drive.",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "Lately a similar problem has been occuring.  When the computer is",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "powered on the HD light flashes a few times and then I am given",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "the \"no disk to boot from\" icon.  However, upon turing the",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "computer off and on again the drive ALWAYS boots up just fine.  ",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "Furthermore, if instead of turning the power on and off I press the reboot ",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "button the same problem occurs.  But, as I said, turning the power",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "off and on always works.",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "This problem is different from the 1989 boot problem in that before",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "it often required several power off and ons to get it to boot.",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "Does anybody have any suggestions as to what the problem is or how",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "it can be fixed?",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "I'm wondering if it's getting old and requires more time to ",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "\"come up to speed\" now.  Is there a PRAM or SCSI setting that",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "allows me to tell the computer to wait a little longer before ",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "trying to access the HD?",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "Thanks!",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "part": "body",
    "sk": true
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "part": "tail",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "A•••• J. S••••••",
    "part": "tail",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "a•••••••@nickel.ucs.indiana.edu",
    "part": "tail",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "Indiana University",
    "part": "tail",
    "sk": false
   },
   {
    "text": "Computer Science Dept.",
    "part": "tail",
    "sk": false
   }
  ],
  "words": {
   "all": 257,
   "ours": 225,
   "sklearn": 206
  }
 },
